.TH HTTP_BODY_FLUSH 3
.SH NAME
http_body_flush \- write the queued body
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <http.h>
.P
.BI "ssize_t http_body_flush(http* " h ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION

.BR http_body_flush ()
writes what http_body(3), http_chunk(3) and http_chunk_end(3) queued as far as the socket takes it. It is called by http_sendreq(3) and http_canwrite(3), also by hand. The data is written to the socket directly, not through the output buffer, so what the socket does not take is not lost.
.SH RETURN VALUE
1 when all is out, 0 when the socket is full, -1 on an error.
.SH SEE ALSO
http_canwrite(3)
